<!--CLI Capability — UpdateProject
  FQN: org.blockml.bml.cli.capability.UpdateProject-->
<clicap:UpdateProject xmlns="http://blockml.org/bml"
  xmlns:cliapi="org.blockml.bml.cli.api"
  xmlns:clicap="org.blockml.bml.cli.capability"
  xmlns:clicommand="org.blockml.bml.cli.command"
  xmlns:clidocumentation="org.blockml.bml.cli.documentation"
  xmlns:core="org.blockml.bml.core">

  <baseType>
    core:Capability
  </baseType>
  <is>
    Point an existing BlockML project at this CLI's versions
  </is>
  <documentation>
    # Point an existing BlockML project at this CLI's versions

    Public entry updateProject(options) → { code, lines }. blockml update parses
    flags, calls this capability, and prints lines. An unexpected positional
    argument is rejected by the command, which also prints the short USAGE.
    This capability does not.

    A project is BlockML when package.json has a blockml key. A missing
    package.json, a package.json without that key, or an unreadable
    package.json returns code 2 and writes nothing.

    Version source is this CLI's own package.json, the same source init uses
    when it first adds the pins. @blockml/cli is ^ plus this CLI's version.
    @blockml/core is the range this CLI declares in dependencies.

    Each pin is updated in the dependency field that already holds it
    (dependencies, devDependencies, peerDependencies, optionalDependencies).
    A missing @blockml/cli is added to devDependencies. A missing @blockml/core
    is added to dependencies. A specifier that contains ":" (workspace:, file:,
    npm:, git, http, and the like) stays as authored. When every registry range
    already matches, package.json is left byte for byte and the result is code 0.

    Unless noInstall, runs npm install in rootDir after a successful rewrite.
    npm install still runs when the ranges were already current. noInstall
    skips that install. Writes package.json only. Leaves BML files, AGENTS.md,
    and CLAUDE.md unchanged. Does not load blockml.config.json.
  </documentation>
  <references>
    <see type="cliapi:UpdateProjectOptions" relation="SeeAlso" />
    <see type="cliapi:UpdateProjectResult" relation="SeeAlso" />
    <see type="clidocumentation:UpdateCommand" relation="SeeAlso" />
    <see type="clicommand:UpdateCommand" relation="SeeAlso" />
    <see type="clicap:InitProject" relation="SeeAlso" />
  </references>
  <properties>
    <options type="cliapi:UpdateProjectOptions">
      <documentation>
        rootDir, optional noInstall. (required)
      </documentation>
    </options>
    <result type="cliapi:UpdateProjectResult">
      <documentation>
        Exit code and structured lines. (required)
      </documentation>
    </result>
  </properties>
</clicap:UpdateProject>
